        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Any method on this page will clear the weeds out of your driveway cracks for a while. Pulling and boiling water are free, flame and vinegar are fast, glyphosate reaches the roots, and a residual product buys a season of bare ground if nothing you value grows nearby.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            What actually ends the cycle is the step after the weed killer: dig out the debris, let the crack dry, and fill it with the right product for asphalt, concrete or pavers. A sealed crack does not grow weeds.
          </p>
